#26.12
    -- ERF no longer uses EKAT. RRTMGP's Kokkos now comes from the new Submodules/kokkos
       submodule (Kokkos 5.1.0, the version EKAT bundled, so answers do not change), and
       Submodules/ekat is gone; run git submodule update --init Submodules/kokkos after
       pulling. GNU Make: EKAT_HOME, BUILD_EKAT and the other EKAT_* variables are now
       ERF_KOKKOS_HOME, ERF_BUILD_KOKKOS and ERF_KOKKOS_* (a generic KOKKOS_HOME in the
       environment is not read), the bundled install moves to
       Submodules/kokkos/build/<config>, and a makefile or command line that still sets an
       EKAT_* variable stops with an error. ERF_KOKKOS_HOME must point at a plain Kokkos
       install. CMake: ERF_ENABLE_EKAT is gone (ERF_ENABLE_RRTMGP enables Kokkos), and
       -DKokkos_ROOT selects an installed Kokkos instead of the submodule. RRTMGP no longer
       links EKAT or spdlog. Build/GNU_Ekat is now Build/GNU_Kokkos

    -- The EAMxx SHOC is removed; native SHOC (erf.pbl_type = NATIVE_SHOC) is the only
       SHOC. erf.pbl_type = SHOC, which used to select the EAMxx SHOC, now selects native
       SHOC and warns that its meaning changed. erf.pbl_type = EAMXX_SHOC, the EAMxx-only
       inputs erf.shoc.apply_tms and erf.shoc.check_flux_state, and the build options
       ERF_ENABLE_EAMXX_SHOC, ERF_ENABLE_SHOC, USE_EAMXX_SHOC and USE_SHOC now stop with an
       error. ERF no longer needs the external E3SM sources (Build/GNU_Ekat/eamxx_clone.sh
       and the SHOC build scripts are gone); EKAT stays, for RRTMGP. The Spack recipe keeps
       +eamxx_shoc for ERF 26.09 to 26.11 only

    -- With several input soundings (erf.input_sounding_file and erf.input_sounding_time),
       the base state, the initial state and the surface layer's surface temperature and
       moisture come from the first sounding. They came from the surface line of the last
       file, combined with the profiles of the first. Every sounding must now have the
       surface pressure of the first; their surface theta and qv may differ and are used
       as nudging targets. A run that reads the soundings stops if the files and times do
       not pair up one to one, or if the times do not increase; it used to drop the extra
       files or times without a word. erf.most.pot_surf_temp and erf.most.surf_moist are checked against the first
       sounding only (#5152)

    -- The YSU PBL-height floor is the top face of the first fluid cell (at least 10 m)
       on every mesh type. Terrain-fitted and stretched meshes keep their answers at the
       default inputs. On constant-dz meshes the floor moves from dz/2 to dz, so pblh and
       the terms that scale with it change in columns that sit on the floor.
       erf.enable_ysu_terrain_pblh_floor is removed; a deck that sets it stops (#5254)

    -- The MRF PBL-height floor is the same as the YSU one: the top face of the first fluid
       cell (at least 10 m) on every mesh type. It was the first cell center (at least
       10 m). pblh and the turbulent length scale change in MRF columns that sit on the
       floor, and in their neighbours with erf.enable_pblh_smoothing. The other fields
       change there when the surface heat flux is not zero. Readers of the stored pblh
       (erf.ibseb.z_i_mode = pblh, the depth of the nest perturbations) see the new
       value. Decks with a first cell of 10 m or less keep their answers (#5258)

    -- WRF nests at level 2 and above are placed relative to the whole parent file, not to
       the parent's ERF region, so a deck with three or more levels that crops level 1 and
       was tuned to the old placement now refines a different region (#4992). Such a nest
       must fit inside the cropped parent region (ERF aborts otherwise), and a nest that
       starts above the bottom of the domain now takes the file's layers at their own
       heights (#4995)

    -- Two-stream radiation sees the immersed-boundary buildings: no heating in solid
       cells, the ground under a footprint held, the shaded ground without the direct
       beam. On by default with erf.ibseb.enable; erf.ibseb.two_stream_buildings = false
       keeps the previous answers (#5004)

    -- Structure models are told the level's step, the stop time, max_step and whether a
       level is fully compressible at initialize(), and get a finalize() call at the end
       of the run. StructureStep::dt is now double: in single precision, out-of-tree
       models that pass it where a Real is expected (e.g. std::min(Real, step.dt)) need
       a static_cast<amrex::Real>, and plug-ins must be rebuilt (#5085)

    -- The surface layer stores and interpolates SST/TSK in K, then converts them to
       potential temperature with current local model surface pressure (#5123). Checkpoints
       use surface_temperature_contract 2; older potential-temperature arrays are migrated
       using checkpoint init provenance. WRFInput migration reads local PSFC regions, with
       parent pressure filling fine-level gaps. Fine-level migration is approximate where
       RemakeLevel may have replaced values with parent-interpolated potential temperature:
       checkpoints do not record per-cell source provenance, and pressure conversion does
       not commute with spatial interpolation. Metgrid version-1 migration uses diagnosed
       ground pressure on ground-touching boxes and parent ground pressure for aloft-only
       boxes; the original input pressure is unavailable. These limits are reported on
       restart. Markerless Metgrid checkpoints remain supported, unused placeholders are
       preserved, and invalid active values fail with a diagnostic.

    -- There is now one YSU PBL scheme: erf.pbl_type = YSU selects the scheme formerly
       called YSUNew, and the original YSU, which was incomplete (it aborted in unstable
       conditions), has been removed. A run that set erf.pbl_type = YSU gets different
       answers. YSUNew is still accepted, with a deprecation warning, for erf.pbl_type and
       erf.most.pblh_calc, and gives the same answers as before. erf.pbl_ysu_force_over_water
       and erf.pbl_ysu_unst_Ribcr, which only the original YSU read, now abort if set.
       With YSU a static refinement box must now span the whole column, as with the other
       PBL schemes: a YSUNew run whose refinement boxes did not, which was allowed before,
       now aborts.

    -- erf.most.pblh_calc = YSU or MRF now aborts unless erf.pbl_type is the same scheme
       on every level. Those PBL heights come from the PBL scheme, so with any other
       erf.pbl_type the height kept its initial bogus value.

